<regions>
<region region-id="1" left="18.00" top="28.00" width="572.00" height="22.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="43.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Heading 1" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Wall steel and annular pile rings</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="2" left="18.00" top="56.00" width="572.00" height="56.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="66.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Fixed scalar units: inches, kip, ksi, with density in kip/ft^3 and areas per foot as labeled. Units are labels, not native dimensional quantities. This sheet recomputes the exported topology. Regenerate after changing pile/row counts, bar size/coating, automatic spacing, or contact assumptions. Two continuous top/bottom fillets. Values are not design acceptance. Case 5778a133d8f0.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="3" left="18.00" top="118.00" width="572.00" height="43.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="128.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">SHARING: Midplane tributaries assign vertical force and the ring rows share the pile-head moment equally; all rings are assumed to engage. Concrete transfer (including concrete below rings), splitting/breakout and row compatibility need a separately substantiated load path.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="4" left="18.00" top="167.00" width="572.00" height="56.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="177.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">STIFFNESS: Ring moments follow pile-head rotational stiffness against the rigid-wall rotation (D-070). The free length to fixity and the axial spring length are entered values (defaults from the pier pile case with sand depth to fixity, LRFD 10.7.3.13.4; tip elevation pending). Lateral, thermal, unsymmetric and construction-stage rotations enter only through the imposed rotation input.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="5" left="18.00" top="229.00" width="572.00" height="30.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="239.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">SCOPE: Wall checks cover minimum shrinkage/temperature steel and detailing only. Wall flexure, shear, lateral loads, seismic and strength load paths are outside this calculation.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="6" left="18.00" top="265.00" width="572.00" height="30.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="275.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">CONNECTION: Local plate and double-fillet checks do not establish pipe-shell bending/ovalization, global pile interaction, ring-segment splices, fatigue, corrosion or WPS/fabrication adequacy.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="7" left="18.00" top="301.00" width="572.00" height="30.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="311.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">BASIS: Confirm geometry, exposure/cover, material grades, construction joints and bar anchorage routing. Starting dimensions are the earlier study snapshot, not a current CAD import.</p></text>
</region>
<region region-id="8" left="18.00" top="337.00" width="178.41" height="17.00" align-x="18.00" align-y="348.00" show-border="false" show-highlight="false" is-protected="true" z-order="0" background-color="inherit" tag="">
